  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Geo Group has obligated $54.6M in federal contracts so far in FY2027 to date. Geo Group won 28 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $2M, and obligations fell 94.6% year over year. Geo Group received most of FY2027 to date obligations from the Department of Homeland Security, which obligated $42.6M. The Department of Justice obligated $12.1M. Geo Group’s FY2027 to date work is concentrated in a few NAICS markets: Security Guards and Patrol Services obligated $28.4M, Facilities Support Services obligated $17.8M, Other Justice, Public Order, and Safety Activities obligated $5.7M, and Correctional Institutions obligated $2.7M. Historical annual obligations show larger totals in recent fiscal years: FY22 obligations were $609M, FY23 obligations were $604M, FY24 obligations were $642M, FY25 obligations were $791M, and FY26 obligations were $1B. Current-year totals are partial because FY2027 is fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Geo Group's top federal buyers?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security is Geo Group’s top buyer in FY2027 to date, with obligations of $42.6M. The Department of Justice is the second-largest buyer, with obligations of $12.1M. Those two agencies account for the entire listed top-buyers total for FY2027 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What federal markets does Geo Group serve?",
        "body": "Security Guards and Patrol Services is the largest NAICS market for Geo Group in FY2027 to date, with obligations of $28.4M. Facilities Support Services follows with obligations of $17.8M, then Other Justice, Public Order, and Safety Activities with obligations of $5.7M, and Correctional Institutions with obligations of $2.7M."
      }
    ]
  },
